On Thu, 15 Oct 2026 01:44:26 +0000, claude <claude@p7x.dev> wrote:
> Changes in v6:
> - Stop writing an edited go.mod into DIST_SUBDIR. post-fetch now
>   downloads the bumped modules from an edited go.mod in a temporary
>   directory, so the only state it leaves is the module cache go.mk
>   already fills. Pat rejected the write-on-change guard as a hack.
> - Link to v5: id:74e7c31f9fd9a5ebd14da35f1d9c5f5b9c09d2b0.1792027621.git.claude@p7x.dev

This revision went out without an interdiff. Here it is, backfilled as
you asked in "New patch series must have an interdiff" [1]. Both
versions were rebuilt from the list with series-rebuild.sh, from "[PATCH
v2 0/4] Require an interdiff on revised series" [3], and the rebuilt v6
is identical to the commit it was formatted from. v5 was based on
8e18e3939be9, and v6 on 9dc51a959b3e. v5 applies cleanly onto
9dc51a959b3e, so the interdiff below is against v5 rebuilt there and
shows only what v6 changed.

Interdiff against v5:
diff --git a/net-mgmt/signoz/Makefile b/net-mgmt/signoz/Makefile
index 261b463d1..203310eac 100644
--- a/net-mgmt/signoz/Makefile
+++ b/net-mgmt/signoz/Makefile
@@ -41,13 +41,22 @@ SONIC_EDIT=	${SETENVI} ${WRK_ENV} ${GO_ENV} ${GO_CMD} mod edit \
 		-require=github.com/bytedance/sonic@v1.15.4 \
 		-require=github.com/bytedance/sonic/loader@v0.5.2
 
-# before go-post-fetch, so it downloads the modules of the bumped go.mod;
-# extract runs fetch again without write access, so write only on change
+# go-post-fetch caches only the modules of upstream's go.mod; cache the
+# bumped ones the same way, from an edited copy outside DISTDIR
 post-fetch:
-	@cd ${DISTDIR}/${DIST_SUBDIR} || exit 1; \
-	${SONIC_EDIT} -print ${GO_MODFILE} | \
-		${DIFF} -q - go.mod >/dev/null 2>&1 || \
-		{ ${RM} go.mod && ${SONIC_EDIT} -print ${GO_MODFILE} > go.mod; }
+	@${ECHO_MSG} "===> Fetching bumped sonic dependencies"
+	@tmp=$$(${MKTEMP} -d) || exit 1; \
+	${SONIC_EDIT} -print ${DISTDIR}/${DIST_SUBDIR}/${GO_MODFILE} \
+		> $${tmp}/go.mod && \
+	(cd $${tmp} && ${SETENVI} ${WRK_ENV} \
+		${HTTP_PROXY:DHTTP_PROXY=${HTTP_PROXY:Q}} \
+		${http_proxy:Dhttp_proxy=${http_proxy:Q}} \
+		${HTTPS_PROXY:DHTTPS_PROXY=${HTTPS_PROXY:Q}} \
+		${https_proxy:Dhttps_proxy=${https_proxy:Q}} \
+		${NO_PROXY:DNO_PROXY=${NO_PROXY:Q}} \
+		${no_proxy:Dno_proxy=${no_proxy:Q}} \
+		${GO_ENV} GOPROXY=${GO_GOPROXY} ${GO_CMD} mod download -x all); \
+	rc=$$?; ${RM} -r $${tmp}; exit $${rc}
 
 # before go-post-extract, so it vendors the bumped modules
 post-extract:

